      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When moving bicycles in Shahbad, the choice between an enclosed containerized carrier and an open trailer can make a decisive difference in how well the bikes are shielded from the harsh realities of highway travel.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>An enclosed carrier functions like a mobile garage: its solid walls and roof block flying stones, rain, dust, and even opportunistic vandalism.</span></li></ul>
<p>By contrast, an open trailer leaves the bike exposed, relying only on straps and tarps that can be torn or blown away, which means the rider must accept a higher risk of scratches, corrosion, and theft.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
