    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Containerized carriers are built with steel or reinforced aluminum panels that absorb impact, while open trailers expose frames and components to direct hits that can dent rims or bend forks.</p>
