      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Shahbad Insured</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When arranging bike transportation in Shahbad, having the correct paperwork is not just a formality – it is a prerequisite for smooth clearance, insurance coverage and legal compliance. The first document you should secure is a self‑attested photocopy of the registration certificate (RC).</p>
<p>This copy must be signed and stamped by the owner and should match the original RC in every detail. It proves ownership and allows the carrier to verify the bike’s identity at every checkpoint.</p>

<p>Next, the current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate is mandatory. The PUC must be issued within the last 30 days and should be valid for the entire duration of the transit. A fresh PUC demonstrates that the bike meets environmental standards and prevents delays at customs or transport authorities.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The third essential piece of paperwork is a valid insurance certificate.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This document must cover the bike against theft, damage and loss for the entire route from Shahbad to the destination.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Ensure that the policy number, coverage limits and effective dates are clearly printed.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>A missing or expired insurance certificate can void the carrier’s liability and expose the owner to financial risk.</span></li></ul>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Finally, obtain an IBA‑approved consignment bilty.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The bilty is the carrier’s receipt of the bike and serves as proof of delivery.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>It must include the consignor’s name, the bike’s chassis number, the agreed freight rate and the terms of transport.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The bilty should be signed by the consignor and the carrier and must be kept in the owner’s records for at least 90 days.</span></li></ul>

<p>Among all these documents, the 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance deserves special emphasis. This type of insurance guarantees that the full market value of the bike is covered in case of loss or damage during sea transit.</p>
<p>By declaring the bike’s value at 100 % of its purchase price, you eliminate the risk of under‑insurance and ensure that any loss is compensated to the full amount. When you present the insurance certificate to the carrier, clearly mark the “100 % declared value” clause to avoid ambiguity during claim processing.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Shahbad</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p><strong>Destination Delivery Handover for Two-Wheeler &amp; Motorcycle: Daylight Condition Re-inspection Against Pickup Photos, Odometer Verification Against the LR Bill of Lading, and Signed Condition Sign-off</strong></p>

<p>When it comes to the seamless delivery of two-wheelers and motorcycles, ensuring a thorough and accurate handover process is crucial. This detailed guide outlines the essential steps to be taken during the destination delivery in daylight conditions, utilizing pickup photos, verifying the odometer, and obtaining a signed condition sign-off from the recipient.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Daylight Condition Re-inspection:</strong></span></li>
</ul>

<p>To ensure the delivered motorcycle or two-wheeler matches the condition described in the pickup photos and meets the expectations of the recipient, perform a re-inspection in daylight conditions.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Ensure the motorcycle or two-wheeler is located in a well-lit area to detect any potential damages or discrepancies.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Check the following areas:<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Exterior: Examine the paintwork, any scratches, dents, or missing parts.</span></li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Interior: Assess the condition of the seat, handlebars, gears, and any other relevant components.</span></li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Undercarriage: Inspect the wheels, tires, and any other undercarriage components.</span></li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Electrical System: Ensure all lights, indicators, and accessories are functioning properly.</span></li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Engine Components: Check the engine, exhaust system, and other essential components for any damages.</span></li>
  </ul></span></li>
</ul>

<p>If any discrepancies are found, document the issues along with photographic evidence and take note of the corresponding pickup photos for comparison.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer Verification:</strong></span></li>
</ul>

<p>Verify the mileage displayed on the odometer against the details provided in the Load Report (LR) and Bill of Lading (BOL):</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Locate the odometer reading on the LR and BOL.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare the recorded odometer reading with the current mileage displayed on the motorcycle or two-wheeler.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If the mileage differs significantly, involve the recipient or authorized personnel to resolve the discrepancy before finalizing the delivery.</span></li>
</ul>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed Condition Sign-off:</strong></span></li>
</ul>

<p>To ensure a smooth handover and avoid any disputes, it is crucial to obtain a signed condition sign-off from the recipient or authorized personnel:</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Collect the recipient's signature on the LR and BOL to acknowledge the motorcycle or two-wheeler's condition upon delivery.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Make sure to clearly document any visible damages or issues in the sign-off process, ensuring both parties are aware of any pre-existing damages.</span></li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Be sure to provide copies of the signed LR and BOL for both parties for future reference.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>By following these procedures, you can ensure a comprehensive inspection, accurate odometer verification, and transparent communication between the delivery team and the recipient, thereby minimizing the risk of any potential disputes.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



